sec.p:
We examined the point estimates, I2 statistics and Cochran’s Q test P-values for the MV and MR associations and found little evidence for heterogeneity between ALSPAC, BiB South Asians and BiB White Europeans (Additional file 1: Supplementary information S14). We therefore meta-analysed estimates from the three samples using a fixed effects model. Results were similar when we instead used a random effects model. For the meta-analyses, we used the ratio estimator (calculated as the meta-analysed PRS-outcome regression coefficient \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
